PART A – PROJECT INTRODUCTION AND VISION

1. Project Overview

Develop a comprehensive, integrated, scalable and secure digital platform for PIHU (Pan India Helping Unit), combining an institutional NGO website, customer applications, seller applications, an e-commerce marketplace, an NGO management system and a centralised administrative platform.

PIHU is a proposed integrated rural development initiative designed to connect rural communities, Self-Help Groups (SHGs), women entrepreneurs, farmers, manufacturers, sellers, volunteers, beneficiaries, consumers and institutional development partners.

The digital platform should support the development of a coordinated rural economic ecosystem through:

1. Rural entrepreneurship development.
2. Women and SHG empowerment.
3. Village Mother Group (VMG) formation and management.
4. One Village One Product (OVOP) development.
5. Rural manufacturing and micro-enterprises.
6. Agriculture and raw-material banking.
7. Seed Bank and Beej Bhandaran initiatives.
8. Rural marketplace and multi-vendor e-commerce.
9. Product quality awareness and traceability.
10. Rural logistics and supply-chain management.
11. Community welfare and education support.
12. Government scheme awareness and facilitation.
13. Institutional, NGO and CSR partnerships.

The platform should be designed for an initial pilot in Hazaribagh district, Jharkhand, with the technical capacity to expand to other districts and states.

2. Main Development Objective

Create one integrated PIHU digital ecosystem with separate interfaces for the public, customers, sellers, volunteers, members, NGO administrators and super administrators.

The platform should connect community development activities with digital commerce while maintaining proper financial records, data security, transparency, accountability and operational control.

The platform must be scalable and modular so that new districts, villages, SHGs, products, sellers, users and development programmes can be added in the future.

